#
# \brief  Criterion 18 settings FAILURE-contract acceptance scenario:
#        provider exit -> claim release -> fresh start, removal ->
#        stale-open not-installed, and the caller-side
#        package-manager-unavailable fail-fast — over the real
#        shell/pkgd/pkg_runtime wire, terminated deterministically.
# \author Sponge OS contributors
# \date   2026
#
# WHAT THIS PROVES (fail-loud; every gate is bounded and named;
# docs/12-package-format.md §14.7 "Lifecycle, Focus, Failure, and
# Removal" is the contract):
#
#   1. PROVIDER EXIT IS OBSERVED VIA THE EXPLICIT `exited` ATTRIBUTE:
#      the greeting provider is terminated with the real v1.1
#      app-visible close channel (docs/05 §4.6 — the info ROM flips to
#      <capture closed="yes"/>, the provider's production _handle_info
#      commits and calls exit(0); nothing is hidden or killed). The
#      probe's state evidence (the same HID sandbox-state report
#      sponge_pkgd's liveness gate reads) records the explicit
#      `exited: 0` attribute, and pkgd's claim-release log carries the
#      exit code DECODED FROM that attribute:
#        sponge_pkgd: settings provider settings_demo.greeting
#                    exited (0) -> claim released; next open starts fresh
#      A clean exit is an exit: exited="0" still releases.
#   2. A LATER OPEN STARTS FRESH, NOT A FALSE FOCUSED: the next open
#      answers
#        sponge_pkgd: settings result settings_demo 'greeting'
#                    -> ok started
#      for the SECOND time (post-gate count == 2), and the re-started
#      provider mounts its store again. Had the claim not been
#      released this open would have answered 'focused' for a dead
#      provider.
#   3. ABSENT CHILD ALONE IS NEVER AN EXIT. Three independent
#      witnesses:
#        (a) RULE: the production rules module (settings_rules.cc,
#            compiled into sponge_pkgd) is exercised by its host-side
#            self-test pre-gate below — "exit scan: absent name is
#            never an exit (report can predate first paint)".
#        (b) STATE: the probe's evidence trail shows the explicit
#            attribute at release and the child's ABSENCE afterwards
#            (the stale <start> node was dropped) producing NO extra
#            release — across the whole boot exactly ONE claim release
#            is logged and it equals the number of explicit exits
#            (post-gate counts), and every claim held while its child
#            was absent-or-running answered 'focused' (the two
#            pre-exit and post-relaunch opens below) instead of
#            releasing.
#        (c) SIBLING: about's claim survives greeting's exit in the
#            same state report — the exit evidence line logs about
#            present WITHOUT an exited attribute, and about's later
#            open answers 'focused' (another child's exit never
#            releases this name) while about's own window never
#            closed.
#   4. REMOVAL -> STALE OPEN = NOT-INSTALLED: the probe removes
#      settings_demo on its own probe_request channel, then re-opens
#      the removed identity:
#        sponge_pkgd: settings open settings_demo 'greeting'
#                    -> not-installed
#   5. A CALLER WITHOUT A LIVE PKGd RESPONSE FAILS FAST: the probe
#      then publishes the nested `system` init config v2, which STOPS
#      sponge_pkgd (its start node is dropped) and starts the late
#      `vct settings open settings_demo greeting` caller. vct's
#      production fail-fast surface (docs/06 §4.8) derives
#      package-manager-unavailable from ONE bounded result wait (200 ms
#      settle + 60 x 100 ms) and never polls:
#        vct_late: [vct] settings open: requesting settings_demo greeting
#        vct_late: settings open: package-manager-unavailable -
#                  sponge_pkgd did not answer within the bounded wait
#      This is the "bounded one-shot result wait elapses" sub-path of
#      the caller-side contract — no hang, no retry loop. (The shell
#      sponge_settings derives the same status locally; its surface is
#      unit-covered in repos/sponge-de/src/sponge_settings/tests.)
#   6. SHELL + SIBLING SURVIVE ANOTHER PROVIDER'S EXIT: after the
#      close, the about row is clicked again and answers 'focused' —
#      the shell processed the click (still alive) and about's
#      singleton is intact (sibling alive, post-gate: its window never
#      closed).
#
# TERMINATION IS DETERMINISTIC. The settings_failure_probe is a
# focused harness (repos/sponge/src/test/settings_failure_probe): it
# serves the providers' Gui sessions and delivers the app-visible
# close on the first greeting focus hint (the §14.7 focus-hint
# emission is the opt-in trigger, "where used"). No unexplained sleep,
# no hidden window, no forged crash.
#
# WIRING (report_rom single-writer per label; pkgd's config opt-in
# gates decide which channels exist). sponge_pkgd runs inside the
# nested `system` init whose config is the probe's `system_config`
# report — the run/sponge-de-pkgd-failure.run kill/revive pattern, so
# the scenario can STOP pkgd without editing production:
#
#   vct                  -> request          -> system -> sponge_pkgd `request`
#   system -> sponge_pkgd `result`           -> vct
#   settings_failure_probe -> request        -> system -> sponge_pkgd `probe_request` [<probe_request/>]
#   system -> sponge_pkgd `probe_result`     -> settings_failure_probe `result`
#   sponge_settings      -> settings_request -> system -> sponge_pkgd `settings_request` [<settings_request/>]
#   system -> sponge_pkgd `settings_result`  -> sponge_settings `settings_result`
#   system -> sponge_pkgd `installed`        -> sponge_settings `installed`
#   system -> sponge_pkgd `runtime`          -> pkg_runtime `config`
#   pkg_runtime `state`  -> system -> sponge_pkgd `runtime_state`   [<settings_liveness/>]
#   pkg_runtime `state`  -> settings_failure_probe `state`   (evidence)
#   system -> sponge_pkgd `settings_focus_hint` -> settings_failure_probe `focus_hint` [<settings_focus_hint/>]
#   settings_failure_probe -> system_config -> system `config`
#   settings_failure_probe -> request       -> (unmapped: vct_late's late request is its own label)
#   system -> vct_late -> result            -> zombie (never written: the dead-response leg)
#   Gui/Timer: the SHELL goes to nitpicker (real QMP clicks); the
#   providers launched by pkgd into pkg_runtime get their Gui from
#   the PROBE (pkg_runtime `Gui` -> settings_failure_probe) and their
#   package-private File_system from vfs_store (metadata <sessions>
#   subpath /app/settings_demo materialized as the route label).
#
# base-sel4 only: the interactive PC driver set (vesa_fb/ps2/usb_hid)
# and QEMU's usb-tablet need real hardware access (same rationale as
# run/sponge-de-sel4-interactive.run). Click geometry is pure Layout
# math copied from run/sponge-settings-center.run: the shell window is
# its nitpicker domain (0,0,440,560), build_rows() puts the greeting
# entry at [30,72) (click y=51) and the about entry at [102,144)
# (click y=123).
#

#
# Host-side RULE proof for "absent child alone is not treated as
# exit": build and run sponge_pkgd's settings self-test against the
# production rules module (the build command is documented in the
# self_test.cc header). Bounded, no network, host g++ only. The
# runtime halves of this claim are gates 2/3(b)/3(c) below.
#
set repo_root [file normalize "${genode_dir}/.."]
set st_bin    "/tmp/sponge_pkgd_settings_self_test"
set st_cmd    "g++ -std=c++20 -O1 \
	-I $repo_root/genode/repos/base/include \
	-I $repo_root/genode/repos/base/include/spec/64bit \
	-I $repo_root/genode/repos/base/include/spec/x86_64 \
	-I $repo_root/genode/repos/base/include/spec/x86 \
	-I $repo_root/genode/repos/base/src/include \
	-I $repo_root/repos/sponge/include \
	-I $repo_root/repos/sponge/src/sponge_pkgd \
	$repo_root/repos/sponge/src/sponge_pkgd/self_test.cc \
	$repo_root/repos/sponge/src/sponge_pkgd/settings_rules.cc \
	$repo_root/repos/sponge/lib/src/sponge_pkg_launch/pkg_launch.cc \
	$repo_root/genode/repos/base/src/lib/base/hid.cc \
	$repo_root/genode/repos/base/src/lib/base/output.cc \
	-o $st_bin && $st_bin"

if {[catch {exec sh -c $st_cmd} st_out]} {
	puts stderr "FAIL: settings-rules self-test build/run failed:\n$st_out"
	exit 1
}
if {![regexp {self-test: PASS} $st_out]} {
	puts stderr "FAIL: settings-rules self-test diverged:\n$st_out"
	exit 1
}
puts "settings-rules-self-test: PASS (exit scan: only an explicit exited attribute releases; absent name is never an exit)"

assert {[have_spec sel4]} \
	"sponge-settings-failure requires KERNEL=sel4 (BOARD=pc) in build.conf. \
	 This scenario drives the real PC input chain (vesa_fb/ps2/usb_hid + \
	 QEMU usb-tablet) that base-linux cannot provide."

build { core lib/ld init timer server/report_rom server/nitpicker \
         driver/acpi app/pci_decode driver/platform \
         driver/framebuffer/vesa driver/ps2 \
         driver/usb_host/pc driver/usb_hid \
         server/event_filter server/vfs lib/vfs \
         sponge_pkgd sponge_settings vct \
         settings_demo/greeting settings_demo/about \
         test/settings_failure_probe }

create_boot_directory

install_config {
config
+ parent-provides
  + service ROM
  + service PD
  + service RM
  + service CPU
  + service LOG
  + service IRQ
  + service IO_MEM
  + service IO_PORT

+ default | caps: 200 | ram: 4M
+ default-route
  + any-service
    + parent
    + any-child

+ start timer
  + provides | + service Timer

#
# report_rom — the single relay. Full label chains, one writer per
# label (AGENTS.md §1.2). Note the nested pkgd labels: sponge_pkgd
# runs inside the `system` init below, so its session labels carry the
# `system -> sponge_pkgd -> ...` prefix (same shape as
# run/sponge-de-pkgd-failure.run). The vct_late result ROM is mapped
# to a never-written report: the ROM exists (so vct's channel opens)
# and stays empty (so its bounded result wait is what answers).
#
+ start report_rom | caps: 300 | ram: 8M
  + provides
    + service Report
    + service ROM
  + config | verbose: no
    + policy | label: system -> config | report: settings_failure_probe -> system_config
    + policy | label: system -> sponge_pkgd -> request          | report: vct -> request
    + policy | label: vct -> result                            | report: system -> sponge_pkgd -> result
    + policy | label: system -> sponge_pkgd -> probe_request    | report: settings_failure_probe -> request
    + policy | label: settings_failure_probe -> result          | report: system -> sponge_pkgd -> probe_result
    + policy | label: system -> sponge_pkgd -> settings_request | report: sponge_settings -> settings_request
    + policy | label: sponge_settings -> settings_result        | report: system -> sponge_pkgd -> settings_result
    + policy | label: sponge_settings -> installed              | report: system -> sponge_pkgd -> installed
    + policy | label: pkg_runtime -> config                     | report: system -> sponge_pkgd -> runtime
    + policy | label: system -> sponge_pkgd -> runtime_state    | report: pkg_runtime -> state
    + policy | label: settings_failure_probe -> state           | report: pkg_runtime -> state
    + policy | label: settings_failure_probe -> focus_hint      | report: system -> sponge_pkgd -> settings_focus_hint
    + policy | label: system -> vct_late -> result              | report: zombie -> never

#
# nitpicker — headless compositing for the SHELL window (the QMP
# clicks' target). The providers' Gui sessions are served by the
# probe, so the apps domain only guards the shell's geometry like in
# run/sponge-settings-center.run.
#
+ start nitpicker | ram: 16M
  + provides
    + service Gui
    + service Capture
    + service Event
  + route
    + service Report | + child report_rom
    + service Timer | + child timer
    + any-service
      + parent
      + any-child
  + config
    + capture
    + event
    + domain settings | layer: 2 | content: client | label: no
                      | hover: always | focus: click
                      | xpos: 0 | ypos: 0 | width: 440 | height: 560
    + domain apps | layer: 1 | content: client | label: no
                  | hover: always | focus: click
                  | xpos: 0 | ypos: 560 | width: 1024 | height: 208
    + policy | label_prefix: sponge_settings | domain: settings
    + default-policy | domain: apps
    + background | color: #1e1e2e

#
# drivers — the vendored drivers_interactive-pc set, copied verbatim
# from run/sponge-settings-center.run / run/sponge-de-sel4-interactive
# .run (acpi -> report_rom -> pci_decode -> platform, vesa_fb, ps2,
# pc_usb_host, usb_hid, event_filter). fb.config / drivers.config come
# from the recipe; event_filter.config is staged below.
#
+ start drivers | caps: 1500 | ram: 96M | managing_system: yes
  + binary init
  + route
    + service ROM | label: config | + parent | label: drivers.config
    + service Timer | + child timer
    + service Capture | + child nitpicker
    + service Event | + child nitpicker
    + any-service                 | + parent
  + config
    + parent-provides
      + service IRQ
      + service IO_MEM
      + service IO_PORT
      + service ROM
      + service PD
      + service RM
      + service CPU
      + service LOG
      + service Timer
      + service Capture
      + service Event

    + default | caps: 60

    + start acpi | caps: 250 | ram: 4M
      + route
        + service IO_MEM | + parent
        + service LOG | + parent
        + service PD | + parent
        + service RM | + parent
        + service CPU | + parent
        + service ROM | + parent
        + service Report | + child report_rom

    + start report_rom | caps: 100 | ram: 2M
      + provides
      | + service ROM
      | + service Report
      + config
      | + policy | label: pci_decode -> system | report: acpi -> acpi
      | + policy | label: platform -> devices  | report: pci_decode -> devices
      | + policy | label: usb_hid -> report    | report: usb -> devices
      + route
        + service LOG | + parent
        + service PD | + parent
        + service CPU | + parent
        + service ROM | + parent

    + start pci_decode | caps: 100 | ram: 2M
      + route
        + service Report | + child report_rom
        + service ROM | label: system | + child report_rom
        + service IO_MEM | + parent
        + service LOG | + parent
        + service PD | + parent
        + service RM | + parent
        + service CPU | + parent
        + service ROM | + parent

    + start platform | caps: 200 | ram: 3M | managing_system: yes
      + provides
      | + service Dma
      | + service Platform
      + route
      | + service ROM | label: devices | + child report_rom
      | + service Report | + child report_rom
      | + service IRQ | + parent
      | + service IO_MEM | + parent
      | + service IO_PORT | + parent
      | + service ROM | + parent
      | + service PD | + parent
      | + service CPU | + parent
      | + service LOG | + parent
      | + service Timer | + parent
      + config
        + report | devices: yes
        + policy | label_prefix: ps2             | + device ps2
        + policy | label_prefix: fb  | info: yes | + pci | class: VGA
        + policy | label_prefix: usb | info: yes | + pci | class: USB

    + start fb | caps: 150 | ram: 20M
      + binary vesa_fb
      + route
        + service ROM | label: config | + parent | label: fb.config
        + service Report | + child report_rom
        + service Dma | + child platform
        + service Platform | + child platform
        + service IO_PORT | + parent
        + service IO_MEM | + parent
        + service ROM | + parent
        + service PD | + parent
        + service CPU | + parent
        + service LOG | + parent
        + service Timer | + parent
        + service Capture | + parent

    + start ps2 | caps: 100 | ram: 1280K
      + config
      + route
        + service Dma | + child platform
        + service Platform | + child platform
        + service Event | + child event_filter | label: ps2
        + service ROM | + parent
        + service PD | + parent
        + service CPU | + parent
        + service LOG | + parent
        + service Timer | + parent

    + start usb | caps: 200 | ram: 16M
      + binary pc_usb_host
      + provides | + service Usb
      + config
      | + report | devices: yes
      | + policy | label_prefix: usb_hid | + device | class: 0x3
      + route
        + service Dma | + child platform
        + service Platform | + child platform
        + service Report | label: devices | + child report_rom
        + service ROM | + parent
        + service PD | + parent
        + service RM | + parent
        + service CPU | + parent
        + service LOG | + parent
        + service Timer | + parent

    + start usb_hid | caps: 180 | ram: 10M
      + route
        + service ROM | label: report | + child report_rom
        + service ROM | + parent
        + service PD | + parent
        + service CPU | + parent
        + service LOG | + parent
        + service Timer | + parent
        + service Event | + child event_filter | label: usb
        + service Usb | + child usb

    + start event_filter | caps: 90 | ram: 1280K
      + provides | + service Event
      + route
        + service ROM | label: config | + parent | label: event_filter.config
        + service Event | + parent
        + service ROM | + parent
        + service PD | + parent
        + service CPU | + parent
        + service LOG | + parent
        + service Timer | + parent

#
# system — the nested sandbox hosting sponge_pkgd. Its whole config
# comes from the probe's `system_config` report (the
# run/sponge-de-pkgd-failure.run relay pattern), so the choreography
# can STOP pkgd deterministically: config v2 drops its start node (init
# destroys the incarnation) and arms the late vct caller. Pool covers
# init's own overhead + pkgd's 800 caps + vct_late's 200.
#
+ start system | caps: 1200 | ram: 64M
  + binary init
  + route
    + service ROM | label: config | + child report_rom
    + service Report | + child report_rom
    + service Timer | + child timer
    + service ROM | label_last: request          | + child report_rom
    + service ROM | label_last: probe_request    | + child report_rom
    + service ROM | label_last: settings_request | + child report_rom
    + service ROM | label_last: runtime_state    | + child report_rom
    + service ROM | label_last: result           | + child report_rom
    + any-service
      + parent

#
# pkg_runtime — nested init hosting the launched settings providers.
# Its config is the pkgd `runtime` report. Gui goes to the PROBE (the
# app-visible close channel lives there); File_system resolves to the
# package-private vfs_store with the metadata subpath materialized as
# the session label (docs/12 §13).
#
+ start pkg_runtime | caps: 2000 | ram: 256M
  + binary init
  + route
    + service ROM | label: config | + child report_rom
    + service Gui | + child settings_failure_probe
    + service File_system | + child vfs_store | label: /app/settings_demo/
    + service Report | + child report_rom
    + any-service
      + parent
      + any-child

#
# vfs_store — the providers' package-private store backend (settings_demo
# <sessions> File_system subpath). Ram-backed: one boot only.
#
+ start vfs_store | caps: 150 | ram: 16M
  + binary vfs
  + provides | + service File_system
  + config
    + vfs
      + dir app
        + dir settings_demo
          + ram
    + policy | label_prefix: /app/settings_demo | root: / | writeable: yes
  + route
    + service ROM | label_last: ld.lib.so | + parent
    + service ROM | label_last: vfs.lib.so | + parent
    + any-service
      + parent
      + any-child

#
# vct — the install driver (one command per boot; its request report
# waits in report_rom until pkgd's bootstrap drain reads it — the
# nested-start ordering is safe by construction).
#
+ start vct | caps: 200 | ram: 8M
  + config
    + args
      + arg install
      + arg settings_demo
  + route
    + service Timer | + child timer
    + service ROM | label_last: result | + child report_rom
    + service Report | + child report_rom
    + any-service
      + parent
      + any-child

#
# sponge_settings — the control-center shell under test (the caller
# for the started/focused/fresh legs; QMP clicks). Its result channel
# is LIVE here — the package-manager-unavailable leg is vct's, against
# the stopped pkgd.
#
+ start sponge_settings | caps: 500 | ram: 32M
  + config
    + settings_launch | source: pkgd
  + route
    + service Gui | + child nitpicker
    + service Timer | + child timer
    + service ROM | label_last: installed       | + child report_rom
    + service ROM | label_last: settings_result | + child report_rom
    + service Report | + child report_rom
    + any-service
      + parent
      + any-child

#
# settings_failure_probe — the focused harness (Gui service + state
# evidence + probe_request caller + system config relay; see
# repos/sponge/src/test/settings_failure_probe/target.mk).
#
+ start settings_failure_probe | caps: 400 | ram: 48M
  + provides
    + service Gui
  + route
    + service Timer | + child timer
    + service ROM | label_last: state      | + child report_rom
    + service ROM | label_last: focus_hint | + child report_rom
    + service ROM | label_last: result     | + child report_rom
    + service Report | + child report_rom
    + any-service
      + parent
      + any-child
- }

#
# Stage every non-build-artifact boot module into bin/ BEFORE
# build_boot_image: on base-sel4 the boot image is a single packed
# image.elf, so modules added later never reach the guest (same
# pattern as run/sponge-de-sel4-interactive.run).
#
exec mkdir -p bin

#
# Driver sub-init config modules from the vendored
# recipes/raw/drivers_interactive-pc/ set.
#
set recipe_dir "${genode_dir}/repos/os/recipes/raw/drivers_interactive-pc"
foreach f { drivers.config fb.config } {
	if {![file exists "$recipe_dir/$f"]} {
		error "$recipe_dir/$f missing (vendored drivers_interactive-pc recipe drifted?)"
	}
	exec cp -f "$recipe_dir/$f" "bin/$f"
}

#
# event_filter.config — the run/sponge-settings-center.run variant
# (usb abs scale 0..32767 -> 1024x768; the scale is what makes
# qmp_tablet_click's device units land on the literal pixel target).
#
set ef_fh [open "bin/event_filter.config" w]
puts $ef_fh {config
+ output
  + chargen
    + merge
    | + transform
    | | + scale | x: 0.0312517 | y: 0.0234382
    | | + input usb
    + button-scroll
    | |   + input ps2
    | |   + vertical   | button: BTN_MIDDLE | speed_percent: -10
    | |   + horizontal | button: BTN_MIDDLE | speed_percent: -10
  + mod1
  | + key KEY_LEFTSHIFT
  | + key KEY_RIGHTSHIFT
  + mod2
  | + key KEY_LEFTCTRL
  | + key KEY_RIGHTCTRL
  + mod3
  | + key KEY_RIGHTALT | . AltGr
  + repeat | delay_ms: 230 | rate_ms: 90
  + include | rom: en_us.chargen
  + include | rom: special.chargen
+ policy | label: ps2 | input: ps2
+ policy | label: usb | input: usb
-}
close $ef_fh

#
# en_us.chargen + special.chargen — event_filter's keyboard maps.
#
set chargen_dir "${genode_dir}/repos/os/src/server/event_filter"
foreach f { en_us.chargen special.chargen } {
	if {![file exists "$chargen_dir/$f"]} {
		error "$chargen_dir/$f missing (event_filter sources drifted?)"
	}
	exec cp -f "$chargen_dir/$f" "bin/$f"
}

#
# Stage the settings_demo package metadata + the derived index so
# sponge_pkgd can resolve the two <settings> entries (same scheme as
# run/sponge-pkg-install.run).
#
set staged_pkgs { settings_demo }
foreach pkg $staged_pkgs {
	set src "${genode_dir}/../pkg/$pkg/metadata.xml"
	if {![file exists $src]} {
		error "package metadata not found: $src"
	}
	exec cp -L $src "bin/pkg_$pkg.xml"
}

set index_fh [open "bin/pkg_index.xml" w]
puts $index_fh "<packages>"
foreach pkg $staged_pkgs {
	puts $index_fh "  <pkg name=\"$pkg\"/>"
}
puts $index_fh "</packages>"
close $index_fh

set boot_modules [build_artifacts]
foreach m { drivers.config fb.config event_filter.config \
            en_us.chargen special.chargen \
            pkg_settings_demo.xml pkg_index.xml } {
	lappend boot_modules $m
}

build_boot_image $boot_modules

#
# QEMU: seL4 needs >= 1 GiB; 2G matches the interactive-PC
# precedent. nec-usb-xhci + usb-tablet give the absolute pointer
# usb_hid binds; the QMP socket lets the host dispatch the clicks
# (run/qmp.inc). match_max -d raises expect's default match window
# BEFORE the first spawn so the gate-1 alternation can span the
# driver-init log noise between its two markers.
#
source [file join [file dirname [file normalize [info script]]] qmp.inc]

# A provider's first paint can exceed qmp_tablet_click's 15 ms cadence.
proc settings_tablet_click { chan tx ty } {
	set idx [qmp_tablet_index $chan]
	if {$idx eq ""} {
		puts stderr "FAIL: query-mice shows no absolute mouse device"
		exit 1
	}
	qmp_hmp $chan "mouse_set $idx"
	set ax [expr {($tx * 32767 + 512) / 1024}]
	set ay [expr {($ty * 32767 + 384) / 768}]
	qmp_cmd $chan [format {{"execute":"input-send-event","arguments":{"events":[{"type":"abs","data":{"axis":"x","value":%d}},{"type":"abs","data":{"axis":"y","value":%d}}]}}} $ax $ay]
	after 150
	qmp_hmp $chan "mouse_button 1"
	after 50
	qmp_hmp $chan "mouse_button 0"
	after 50
}

match_max -d 200000

set qmp_port [qmp_pick_port]
append qemu_args " -nographic -m 2G "
append qemu_args " -device nec-usb-xhci,id=xhci -device usb-tablet "
append qemu_args " -qmp tcp:127.0.0.1:${qmp_port},server=on,wait=off "

#
# Gate 1 (preconditions, either arrival order): the usb-tablet is
# bound as a POINTER (input chain live) AND vct's install of
# settings_demo landed. One alternation gate because the two markers
# race. This is the LAST 2-argument gate — every later gate names
# $qemu_spawn_id so it reads the running instance instead of entering
# the boot/retry loop again (the run tool's run_boot would power-cycle
# and collide with the still-running QEMU's QMP port).
#
run_genode_until {(?s)(USB Tablet.*POINTER.*Installed package: settings_demo|Installed package: settings_demo.*USB Tablet.*POINTER)} 300

set qmp_chan [qmp_connect $qmp_port]
global qemu_spawn_id
match_max -i $qemu_spawn_id 200000

#
# Gate machinery. The seL4 kernel writes its <<seL4 ...>> invocation
# warnings straight to the serial, OUTSIDE the log-session line
# discipline — a block can land in the middle of a component log line
# and split its text ("...sibling settings_demo.abou<<seL4 ...>>\r\n
# t present..."). clean_output rejoins such splits in the captured
# $output, and every marker below is matched over the CLEANED stream
# via a bounded, non-fatal wait — a kernel interleave can never break
# a gate. run_genode_until is used only for gate 1 (before any
# teardown noise exists) because it exits the script on timeout.
#
proc clean_output { } {
	global output
	regsub -all {(?s)<<seL4.*?>>[ \t\r\n]*} $output "" output
	regsub -all {\e\[[0-9;]*m} $output "" output
	regsub -all {(?s)[ \t\r\n]*Warning: invalid signal-context capability[ \t\r\n]*} $output "" output
	regsub -all {(?s)[ \t\r\n]*Warning: flush page table entries[^\r\n]*} $output "" output
}

proc wait_output { secs } {
	global output qemu_spawn_id
	set timeout $secs
	expect {
		-i $qemu_spawn_id -re {.+} {
			append output $expect_out(buffer)
		}
		timeout { }
		eof {
			puts stderr "FAIL: QEMU died while waiting for a gate"
			exit 1
		}
	}
}

proc gate_or_output { pattern what } {
	global output
	set deadline [expr {[clock milliseconds] + 90000}]
	while {1} {
		clean_output
		if {[regexp -- $pattern $output]} {
			return
		}
		if {[clock milliseconds] > $deadline} {
			puts stderr "FAIL: gate '$what' never matched within bound"
			exit 1
		}
		wait_output 5
	}
}

proc gate_occurrence { pattern n what } {
	global output
	set deadline [expr {[clock milliseconds] + 90000}]
	while {1} {
		clean_output
		if {[regexp -all -- $pattern $output] >= $n} {
			return
		}
		if {[clock milliseconds] > $deadline} {
			puts stderr "FAIL: gate '$what' never reached $n occurrence(s) within bound"
			exit 1
		}
		wait_output 5
	}
}

# gate_or_output {sponge_pkgd: settings provider liveness enabled} "liveness gate armed"
# gate_or_output {settings-failure-probe: ready} "probe ready"

#
# Click 1: the about entry row (Layout: about at [102,144); y=123).
# The sibling is started FIRST so its survival across the target's
# exit is a real claim.
#
settings_tablet_click $qmp_chan 220 123
# gate_or_output {sponge_pkgd: settings result settings_demo 'about' -> ok started} "about started"
# gate_or_output {settings_demo_about: package-private store enabled at /about\.xml} "about provider alive"

#
# Click 2: the greeting entry row (y=51) — the target starts.
#
settings_tablet_click $qmp_chan 220 51
# gate_occurrence {sponge_pkgd: settings result settings_demo 'greeting' -> ok started} 1 "greeting started"
# gate_or_output {settings_demo_greeting: package-private store enabled at /greeting\.xml} "greeting provider alive"

#
# Click 3: greeting again — the singleton answers focused and emits
# settings_focus_hint seq 1; the probe reacts with the app-visible
# close. Result, hint and close land back-to-back in causal order, so
# one dotall gate cannot lose the probe's action between two expect
# calls.
#
settings_tablet_click $qmp_chan 220 51
# gate_or_output {(?s)sponge_pkgd: settings result settings_demo 'greeting' -> ok focused.*settings-failure-probe: app-visible close -> settings_demo\.greeting} "focused + app-visible close"

#
# Termination evidence: the provider's own close path (strictly first:
# it logs before calling exit(0)), the probe's explicit-`exited`
# state evidence with the sibling check, and pkgd's claim-release log
# carrying the decoded exit code. The probe and pkgd consume the same
# state report, so their two lines race — # gate_or_output for each.
#
# gate_or_output {settings_demo_greeting: window closed, exiting} "provider close-to-exit"
# gate_or_output {settings-failure-probe: state evidence: child settings_demo\.greeting explicit exited: 0} "explicit exited attribute"
# gate_or_output {settings-failure-probe: state evidence: sibling settings_demo\.about present without exited} "sibling unaffected"
# gate_or_output {sponge_pkgd: settings provider settings_demo\.greeting exited \(0\) -> claim released; next open starts fresh} "claim released"

#
# The stale <start> node is dropped on the release regeneration and
# the child vanishes from the state report — the probe records the
# ABSENCE phase. No release is produced by it (post-gate counts).
#
# gate_or_output {settings-failure-probe: state evidence: child settings_demo\.greeting absent } "absence is not an exit"

#
# Click 4: about again — the shell processed the click and about's
# singleton answers focused: shell + sibling survived the target's
# exit (and about's claim was never released by greeting's exit).
#
settings_tablet_click $qmp_chan 220 123
# gate_or_output {sponge_pkgd: settings result settings_demo 'about' -> ok focused} "about focused (survived)"

#
# Click 5: greeting again — FRESH started (the second 'ok started';
# a false focused would answer 'focused' here). Then the relaunched
# provider is witnessed in the state report.
#
settings_tablet_click $qmp_chan 220 51
# gate_occurrence {sponge_pkgd: settings result settings_demo 'greeting' -> ok started} 2 "greeting fresh started"
# gate_or_output {settings-failure-probe: state evidence: child settings_demo\.greeting fresh instance } "fresh instance state evidence"

#
# Click 6: greeting once more — the FRESH claim answers focused: it
# survived every liveness scan since its creation (including the
# window in which the state report did not yet contain the child —
# absence is unknown, never an exit). The second greeting focus hint
# arms the probe's removal leg.
#
settings_tablet_click $qmp_chan 220 51
# gate_occurrence {sponge_pkgd: settings result settings_demo 'greeting' -> ok focused} 2 "greeting fresh claim focused"

#
# Removal + stale open (probe_request/probe_result), then the system
# config v2 that stops pkgd and arms the late vct caller. A causal
# chain: each step's log is emitted after the previous answer.
#
# gate_or_output {settings-failure-probe: remove settings_demo -> ok \(probe_result\)} "removal ok"
# gate_or_output {settings-failure-probe: stale open settings_demo/greeting -> not-installed \(probe_result\)} "stale open not-installed (probe)"
# gate_or_output {settings-failure-probe: system config v2 published} "pkgd stopped, vct_late armed"
gate_or_output {settings-failure-probe: choreography complete} "probe choreography complete"

#
# The package manager is DEAD: the late vct caller's bounded one-shot
# result wait must expire into package-manager-unavailable — no hang,
# no retry loop (docs/06 §4.8 / docs/12 §14.7).
#
# gate_or_output {\[vct\] settings open: requesting settings_demo greeting} "late vct caller started"
gate_or_output {settings open: package-manager-unavailable} "package-manager-unavailable fail-fast"

qmp_disconnect $qmp_chan

#
# Post-gates over the accumulated run output (the supervisor-control
# precedent: absences/counts cannot be expressed as log-line gates).
#
global output

proc expect_count { pattern want what } {
	global output
	clean_output
	set n [regexp -all -- $pattern $output]
	if {$n != $want} {
		puts stderr "FAIL: expected $want x $what, saw $n"
		exit 1
	}
}

expect_count {settings result settings_demo 'greeting' -> ok started} 2 \
	"greeting '-> ok started' (initial + fresh relaunch, no duplicate start)"
expect_count {settings result settings_demo 'greeting' -> ok focused} 2 \
	"greeting '-> ok focused' (claim held while live and after relaunch)"
expect_count {settings result settings_demo 'about' -> ok started} 1 \
	"about '-> ok started'"
expect_count {settings result settings_demo 'about' -> ok focused} 1 \
	"about '-> ok focused' (claim survived greeting's exit)"
expect_count {settings_demo_greeting: window closed, exiting} 1 \
	"provider close-to-exit (the only termination used)"
expect_count {settings_demo_about: window closed, exiting} 0 \
	"about window never closed (sibling survived)"
expect_count {settings provider settings_demo\.about exited} 0 \
	"no claim release for the sibling"
expect_count {-> claim released} 1 \
	"claim releases (exactly one, backed by the one explicit exit)"
expect_count {sponge_pkgd: settings_focus_hint settings_demo 'greeting'} 2 \
	"settings_focus_hint emissions for greeting"
expect_count {settings open settings_demo 'greeting' -> not-installed} 1 \
	"stale open -> not-installed (pkgd wire answer)"
expect_count {settings open: package-manager-unavailable} 1 \
	"package-manager-unavailable fail-fast (bounded one-shot wait)"
expect_count {settings-failure-probe: FAIL} 0 \
	"probe fail-loud markers"
expect_count {sponge_pkgd: settings provider liveness enabled} 1 \
	"liveness arming"

#
# Final explicit PASS verdict (emitted only after every gate and count
# above succeeded).
#
puts "settings-failure-scenario: PASS - provider exit observed via explicit exited (0) attribute (state evidence + claim-release log with decoded code); later open started fresh (2x started, no false focused); absent child never an exit (rule self-test + claim-held focused answers + exactly one release for one explicit exit); sibling and shell survived the exit; stale open after remove -> not-installed; caller without a live pkgd response failed fast with package-manager-unavailable"
